# The templates are the CLI's output. Git on Windows converts a checked-out
# text file to CRLF by default, which made the generator emit CRLF there and LF
# everywhere else — two developers on one project producing diffs that differ
# only by line ending, and a Windows CI run failing on an assertion that was
# right about the content.
#
# A generator's output must not depend on the host OS, so every text file in
# this repo stays LF in the working tree on all platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf
